1	# michi-graph
2	
3	Deterministic dependency graphs for dev tools: steps in a pipeline, operations in a release, packages in a workspace, tasks in a plan. MIT-licensed, no dependencies, `no_std` + `alloc`.
4	
5	- **Every problem at once.** Validation reports duplicate nodes, unknown dependencies, self-dependencies and cycles in one list, in a fixed order. Each cycle names all of its members and one concrete loop.
6	- **Deterministic.** Ties break by declaration order or by key, your choice, and every output follows it: the topological order (the smallest valid one), layers, ready sets, closures and cycle reports.
7	- **No recursion.** A 100,000-node chain or cycle validates without touching the stack limit.
8	- **Edge kinds.** Give edges a kind (runtime, dev, …) and choose per validation which kinds count, so one graph yields several dags.
9	
10	```rust
11	use michi_graph::{Dag, Order};
12	
13	let dag = Dag::from_nodes(
14	    [("build", vec![]), ("test", vec!["build"]), ("lint", vec![]), ("ship", vec!["test", "lint"])],
15	    Order::Declaration,
16	)
17	.unwrap();
18	assert_eq!(dag.keys_in_order().copied().collect::<Vec<_>>(), ["build", "test", "lint", "ship"]);
19	
20	let err = Dag::from_nodes([("a", vec!["b"]), ("b", vec!["a"])], Order::Key).unwrap_err();
21	assert_eq!(err.to_string(), "dependency cycle: a depends on b, which depends on a");
22	```
23	
24	With edge kinds:
25	
26	```rust
27	use michi_graph::{GraphBuilder, Order, UnknownTargets};
28	
29	#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, PartialOrd, Ord)]
30	enum Kind { Runtime, Dev }
31	
32	let mut b = GraphBuilder::<&str, Kind>::new();
33	let app = b.node("app");
34	let lib = b.node("lib");
35	b.depends_on(app, "lib", Kind::Runtime);
36	b.depends_on(lib, "app", Kind::Dev); // a dev-only cycle
37	let graph = b.build(UnknownTargets::Error);
38	
39	let runtime = graph.validate_filtered(|e| *e.kind == Kind::Runtime, Order::Key).unwrap();
40	assert_eq!(runtime.keys_in_order().copied().collect::<Vec<_>>(), ["lib", "app"]);
41	assert!(graph.validate(Order::Key).is_err());
42	```
