1	//! # michi-pipeline
2	//!
3	//! Runs a validated graph of async steps on Tokio and returns a [`RunRecord`] saying what happened to each one.
4	//!
5	//! 1. Define steps with [`ExecStep`] (a [`StepId`], a display name, prerequisites, a [`Step`] runner) and validate
6	//!    them into a [`Plan`]. Validation reports every problem at once; [`Plan::execution_order`] is the dry run.
7	//! 2. [`execute`] the plan under a caller-supplied [`RunId`] with [`ExecOptions`]: sequential or parallel with a
8	//!    concurrency cap (overall and per key), skip-dependents or fail-fast, retry policy and budget, timeouts and
9	//!    shared deadlines, keyed circuit breakers, cancellation and a progress observer.
10	//! 3. Read the record: every step has one status from [`michi_core::pipeline::StepStatus`] with a reason, and the
11	//!    run has a [`RunOutcome`] that is `Succeeded` only if every step succeeded.
12	//! 4. [`resume`] an interrupted run from its record under the same run id: finished steps are not re-run, and steps
13	//!    whose outcome is unknown are re-run only if idempotent, prechecked or verified by the caller.
14	//!
15	//! Steps are usually async closures ([`step_fn`]); [`poll_step`] waits for something on a fixed schedule and
16	//! [`step_blocking`] runs blocking work on Tokio's blocking pool.
17	//!
18	//! The replay rule (see [`Step`]) keeps retries and resume from blindly repeating work that may already have taken
19	//! effect: every failure says whether retrying could help and whether its [`Effect`] may have landed, a
20	//! [`Replay::Prechecked`] step looks before it acts ([`Step::precheck`]), and [`ExecOptions::durable_starts`] runs a
21	//! step only once its start is saved. Resume is at least once per step; pass [`StepContext::idempotency_key`] to a
22	//! deduplicating downstream for exactly-once effects. See `docs/spec/08-pipeline-execution.md`.
23	//!
24	//! ```
25	//! use michi_pipeline::{execute, step_fn, ExecOptions, ExecStep, Plan, RunId, RunOutcome, StepId};
26	//!
27	//! # tokio::runtime::Builder::new_current_thread().enable_time().build().unwrap().block_on(async {
28	//! let fetch = StepId::try_new("fetch").unwrap();
29	//! let plan = Plan::new(vec![
30	//!     ExecStep::new(fetch.clone(), "Fetch data", step_fn(|_ctx| async { Ok(()) })),
31	//!     ExecStep::new(StepId::try_new("upload").unwrap(), "Upload", step_fn(|ctx| async move {
32	//!         let _key = ctx.idempotency_key(); // "run-1:upload" on every attempt and on resume
33	//!         Ok(())
34	//!     }))
35	//!     .depends_on(fetch),
36	//! ])
37	//! .unwrap();
38	//! let record = execute(&plan, RunId::try_new("run-1").unwrap(), &ExecOptions::new()).await;
39	//! assert_eq!(record.outcome(), RunOutcome::Succeeded);
40	//! assert_eq!(
41	//!     record.render(),
42	//!     "step[2]{id,name,status,reason}:\n  fetch,Fetch data,completed,null\n  upload,Upload,completed,null"
